  "agent": "claude -p (fresh agent; cwd an empty folder outside the repository holding only a copy of the skill folder without evals; tools Read, Glob, Grep, Bash(node:*))",
  "recordedAt": "2026-11-15",
  "output": "## Accessibility audit: ARIA review\n\nInput: HTML, 8 elements. The script ran 34 checks and found 6 (4 failure, 2 advisory). Not a conformance claim: only the checks listed here ran.\n\n### Findings\n1. **label-in-name** · SC 2.5.3 Label in Name (A) · failure\n   Element: `<button role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Buy now\">` (line 2)\n   Affects: voice control\n   Problem: The accessible name \"Buy now\" does not contain the visible text \"Add to cart\". A voice control user who says the words on the button will not activate it.\n   Fix:\n   ```diff\n   - <button role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Buy now\">Add to cart</button>\n   + <button role=\"button\">Add to cart</button>\n   ```\n\n2. **redundant-role** · SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A) · advisory\n   Element: `<button role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Buy now\">` (line 2)\n   Affects: screen reader\n   Problem: `role=\"button\"` repeats the role that `<button>` already has.\n   Fix:\n   ```diff\n   - <button role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Buy now\">Add to cart</button>\n   + <button aria-label=\"Buy now\">Add to cart</button>\n   ```\n   If you apply both 1 and 2, the line becomes `<button>Add to cart</button>`.\n\n3. **aria-hidden-focusable** · SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A) · failure\n   Element: `<div aria-hidden=\"true\">` (line 3)\n   Affects: keyboard, screen reader\n   Problem: The \"Skip\" link is hidden from screen readers but can still be reached with Tab, so focus lands on something that is never announced.\n   Fix:\n   ```diff\n   - <div aria-hidden=\"true\"><a href=\"/x\">Skip</a></div>\n   + <div><a href=\"/x\">Skip</a></div>\n   ```\n\n4. **native-element** · SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A) · advisory\n   Element: `<span role=\"link\" tabindex=\"0\">` (line 4)\n   Affects: keyboard, screen reader\n   Problem: `role=\"link\"` on a span rebuilds what `<a>` already does, and it needs extra scripts to handle keys and states. A native `<a>` with an `href` gets focus, Enter and the link role without extra code.\n   Fix:\n   ```diff\n   - <span role=\"link\" tabindex=\"0\">Terms</span>\n   + <a href=\"URL of the Terms page\">Terms</a>\n   ```\n\n5. **aria-ref-missing** · SC 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (A) · failure\n   Element: `<input aria-labelledby=\"ghost\">` (line 5)\n   Affects: screen reader\n   Problem: `aria-labelledby` points to the id \"ghost\", and no element has that id, so the field has no name.\n   Fix:\n   ```diff\n   - <input aria-labelledby=\"ghost\">\n   + <input aria-labelledby=\"id-of-an-element-on-the-page\">\n   ```\n   Add that id to the visible text that labels the field. If the field has no visible label, use a native `<label for>` instead.\n\n6. **dialog-name** · SC 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A) · failure\n   Element: `<div role=\"dialog\">` (line 6)\n   Affects: screen reader\n   Problem: The dialog has no accessible name, so a screen reader opens it with no title.\n   Fix:\n   ```diff\n   - <div role=\"dialog\"><p>Are you sure?</p></div>\n   + <div role=\"dialog\" aria-labelledby=\"dialog-title\"><p id=\"dialog-title\">Are you sure?</p></div>\n   ```\n\n### Needs a manual test\n- **Keyboard only:** press Tab through the whole input. Every control should be reachable, the order should follow the reading order and focus should never get trapped (SC 2.1.1, 2.1.2, 2.4.3).\n- **Screen reader** (for example NVDA with Firefox, or VoiceOver with Safari): names, roles, states and headings should be spoken as expected (SC 4.1.2, 1.3.1).\n- **Voice control** (for example Voice Control or Dragon): say each visible label and check that it activates the control (SC 2.5.3).\n- **Zoom and reflow:** set the browser to 200% and to 400% at 1280 CSS px wide (about 320 CSS px). No content should be lost and nothing should need scrolling in two directions (SC 1.4.4, 1.4.10).\n- **Alt text quality:** the script only checks that alt text exists. A person must check that it says what each image is for (SC 1.1.1).\n- **Dialog:**\n  - Opening it moves focus inside.\n  - Tab stays inside while it is open.\n  - Escape closes it.\n  - Focus returns to the button that opened it (SC 2.1.2, 2.4.3).\n- **Forms:** submit with errors and check that the screen reader announces each error and moves to the first one (SC 3.3.1, 4.1.3).\n- **Page-level checks:** language, title, viewport and main landmark were skipped because the input is a fragment. Run them on the full page.\n\n### Not checked here\n- Contrast, focus-ring style, spacing and target size: not checked; ui-polish owns them.\n- Whether the flow makes sense and whether the words are clear: not part of this audit.\n\n### Open questions\n- Finding 4: where should \"Terms\" link to? The input has no URL, so the `href` is a placeholder.\n- Finding 5: what visible text labels the `<input>`? The input does not say, so the id is a placeholder.\n- Finding 3: is the \"Skip\" link meant to be usable? If it should be hidden, add `hidden` or `inert` to the div instead of `aria-hidden`, so it also leaves the Tab order.",
